# RUN PIPELINE STEPS
## Prerequisites
1. Setup your snowflake connection details in your env file and make sure the respective role, datawarehouse, database and schema are configured
```bash
SNOWFLAKE_ACCOUNT = your_account
SNOWFLAKE_USERNAME = your_username
SNOWFLAKE_PASSWORD = your_password
SNOWFLAKE_ROLE = TRANSFORM_ROLE
SNOWFLAKE_WAREHOUSE = TRANSFORM_WH
SNOWFLAKE_DATABASE = HEALTHCARE_ANALYTICS
SNOWFLAKE_RAW_SCHEMA = RAW

#STEPS to setup SNOWFLAKE
RUN scripts in SQL-01_snowflake_setup
```

### Turn on Docker and make sure it is up and running
```bash
# Run the following commands for bringing up APACHE AIRFLOW
# Start Server all containers
docker-compose up -d

# To check all containers health:
docker-compose ps

# Stop Server
docker-compose down

# Start Specific Container
docker-compose up -d snowflake-dbt-pipeline-airflow-worker-1

# Restart particular servers
docker-compose restart airflow-apiserver

# Available Containers List
snowflake-dbt-pipeline-airflow-apiserver-1
snowflake-dbt-pipeline-airflow-triggerer-1
snowflake-dbt-pipeline-airflow-dag-processor-1
snowflake-dbt-pipeline-airflow-scheduler-1
snowflake-dbt-pipeline-redis-1
snowflake-dbt-pipeline-postgres-1

# For checking logs
docker logs snowflake-dbt-pipeline-airflow-worker-1 --tail 100 -f
docker logs snowflake-dbt-pipeline-airflow-apiserver-1 --tail 100 -f
docker logs snowflake-dbt-pipeline-airflow-init-1
docker logs snowflake-dbt-pipeline-airflow-dag-processor-1 --tail 50
```
## Command to create Admin user for accessing airflow
```bash
 docker-compose  exec airflow-apiserver airflow users create --username admin --firstname Admin --lastname User --role Admin --email admin@example.com --password admin
```

